  body: "# Self-employed earner in the JSA and Income Support guidance\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\
    \nThe captured chapter describes gainful employment in Great Britain that is not employed-earner employment,
    and recognises that a person may also have separate employed work.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\n\
    Status requires weighing the source’s factors; no single label or tax arrangement decides it here.
    Directors of limited companies are treated separately as office holders in DMG 27011. Current trading
    status, sickness, cessation and capital assets remain distinct questions. This is not an equivalence
    with the Pension Credit self-employment concept.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 27002,
    PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0f9e520b52e4144868939/dmg-Ch-27.pdf#page=4)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 27: Self-employed earners and share fishermen.\n- [DMG 27005, PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0f9e520b52e4144868939/dmg-Ch-27.pdf#page=4)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 27: Self-employed earners and share fishermen.\n- [DMG 27011, PDF page 6](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0f9e520b52e4144868939/dmg-Ch-27.pdf#page=6)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 27: Self-employed earners and share fishermen.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\n\
    Model-assisted interpretation of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot.
    Specialist review is required. Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this
    record’s authoring time are separate.\n\nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official
    DWP document, individual advice, an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted
    text may alter reading order, footnotes and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage
    or behavioural evaluation pass is claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol5-ch27`: PDF SHA-256 `90b6c5ec739d2366936d67d78cd5a6f857b764b92000200f4a44ac956c88b3ac`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `7f84279f4a44373405ce06d32bf1c927a9f25dda507895b1540e6bb8b1b5185a`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/jsais-employed-earner
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source distinguishes a limited company and its director and identifies the
      director as an employed earner; the association preserves the classification boundary.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol5-ch27/0006
      quote: "27011 A limited company, of whatever size, is separate from its employees, officers and
        shareholders 1.\nThis means that the profits of the company do not belong to the directors. A
        director of a limited\n\ncompany is an office holder in the company2 and is an employed earner
        (see DMG 26048).\n\n\n                                                             1 R(SB) 57/83;
        2 McMillan v Guest 1942, AC 561"
      locator: DMG 27011
  - target: term/jsais-self-employed-assessment-period
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The chapter’s normal-weekly-earnings passage requires receipts and expenses for the
      assessment period of a self-employed earner.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol5-ch27/0014
      quote: "27051 The normal weekly earnings of a S/E earner should be calculated by using the\n\n\n\
        1. gross receipts (see DMG 27125) and\n\n\n2. expenses paid out (see DMG 27190)\n\n\nduring the
        assessment period. Different rules apply for royalties, copyright payments and Public Lending\n\
        Rights payments."
      locator: DMG 27051
